From 94d1ab162fe2c39fd84873df9e2a4d2661c98ca9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 21:19:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 252/258] fix(execution): enforce the in-document witness
 relation of the measured envelope

- manifest.measured_witness_shortfall(): every K cited in measurement_scope.external[*].observed_max_by_k or q8_reference_observed_by_k must appear in measured_deviation_by_k with a value >= the cited witness.  Raising measured_deviation_by_k above every witness is not refutable inside one document and stays a documented irreducible boundary (no check invented for it).
- plan/report validators run the helper on both envelope copies and fail closed with plan_field_inconsistent / report_field_inconsistent, mirroring the proven-bound dominance check.
- tests: four mutation directions (measured below an external witness, measured below the q8 reference, a witness raised above measured, a witness K missing from measured) exercised on plan and report, plus a boundary test that raising the measurement above all witnesses stays accepted.
- binding_verify docstring: artifact.pack.strategy <-> timing.timing_basis.pack_semantics and artifact.library <-> resolved.library are in-document enforced pairs; only value-vs-manifest comparison is a boundary.  Added the unterminated explanation-layer entries (fallback_events[*] payloads, tie_break_key prefixes, parallelism/thread-env knobs) and pointed at brief sections 14-15.
